            cost[i] += min(cost[i + 1], cost[i + 2]);
        }

        // After the loop, cost[0] contains the min cost to reach top starting from step 0.
        // And cost[1] contains the min cost to reach top starting from step 1.
        // Since we can start from either step 0 or step 1, we return the minimum of these two.
